# Class -> Rust path glob (relative to crates/fr-dsn/src) map for scripts/audit-port.sh's
# per-class matching (Plan 3 Task 1 obligation). Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are
# ignored. Append one line per class as later Plan 3 tasks port it; do not remove a class's line
# once a task starts porting it, or the audit falls back to a crate-wide (weaker) check for it.
# A class whose Rust home spans more than one file gets one map line per file — not one line
# with several space-separated globs, which the reader (`read -r cls path`) would only keep the
# first token of.
IdentifierType      format/identifier.rs
IndentFileWriter    format/indent_writer.rs
SpecctraDsnStreamReader  lexer/*.rs
IJFlexScanner            lexer/*.rs
Keyword                  keyword.rs
ScopeKeyword             keyword.rs
ScopeKeyword             parser/scope_parameter.rs
DsnFile                  parser/dsn_file.rs
ReadScopeParameter       parser/scope_parameter.rs
WriteScopeParameter      parser/scope_parameter.rs
BoardParserCallback      parser/scope_parameter.rs
Shape                    parser/geometry.rs
Rectangle                parser/geometry.rs
Circle                   parser/geometry.rs
Polygon                  parser/geometry.rs
Path                     parser/geometry.rs
PolygonPath              parser/geometry.rs
PolylinePath             parser/geometry.rs
Layer                    parser/geometry.rs
# `Layer.writeScope` (Layer.java:48-66) lives with the `structure` writer that is its only
# caller — see `parser/structure.rs` (Plan 3 Task 11).
Layer                    parser/structure.rs
LayerStructure           parser/geometry.rs
Parser                   parser/header.rs
Resolution               parser/header.rs
Unit                     parser/header.rs
CoordinateTransform      coordinate_transform.rs
Structure                parser/structure.rs
Plane                    parser/structure.rs
AutorouteSettings        parser/autoroute_settings.rs
# The plan's File Structure lists `PlaceControl` with `structure.rs`; it lives instead in the
# shared header-scopes file alongside `Parser`/`Resolution`/`Unit` — all four are tiny scopes
# with no dedicated file of their own (Plan 3 Task 6/module docs of `parser/header.rs`).
PlaceControl             parser/header.rs
Library                  parser/library.rs
Package                  parser/library.rs
PartLibrary              parser/part_library.rs
Rule                     parser/network.rs
Placement                parser/placement.rs
Component                parser/placement.rs
ComponentPlacement       parser/placement.rs
Package                  parser/placement.rs
Circuit                  parser/network.rs
NetClass                 parser/network.rs
Net                      parser/network.rs
NetList                  parser/network.rs
Network                  parser/network.rs
KiCadNetClassNames       parser/network.rs
Wiring                   parser/wiring.rs
DsnReader                dsn_reader.rs
DsnWriter                dsn_writer.rs
BoardReadResult          error.rs
BoardMetadata            error.rs
# `io/FileFormat.java` is a bare nine-constant enum with no public methods, so this line only
# keeps it MAPPED. Its **code** home moved to `crates/fr-core/src/job.rs` in Plan 8 Task 1, beside
# its two producers (`RoutingJob.getFileFormat(byte[]/Path)`); scan ruling R17 is why (the plan
# draft had it as a seven-value nested enum of `RoutingJob`). Task 14's `io/` sweep records it.
FileFormat               error.rs
SesWriter                ses_writer.rs
# `SesWriter.formatPlacementRotation` is the package's only `String.format`; it lives with the
# other Java number-formatting emulations (Plan 3 Task 2), not with the writer that calls it.
SesWriter                format/double.rs
SesReader                ses_reader.rs
SesImportSummary         ses_reader.rs
RulesReader              rules_reader.rs
RulesWriter              rules_writer.rs

# --- io/kicad/ (Plan 8 Task 8: the DTO tree and `readBoard`'s sections 1-8) -------------------
#
# The `io/kicad` **audit invocation** runs against `crates/fr-drc/src` with
# `scripts/audit-map/fr-drc.map` (plan-5 ruling 13 put the package there, for the four DRC report
# DTOs), so these two lines are not read by any of the four invocations the crate README lists.
# They are here so that the class -> Rust-file map is recorded where the *code* is, and so Plan 8
# Task 14 can move the invocation to this crate without re-deriving them. `KiCadJsonWriter` gets
# its line from Task 10, which writes it.
KiCadJsonReader          kicad/reader.rs
KiCadBoardJson           kicad/dto.rs

# `SessionToEagle` (io/specctra/parser/SessionToEagle.java, 627 lines) is **out of Plan 3's
# scope** — the plan's Architecture paragraph puts it, with `io/kicad/**`, in Plan 8 ("fr-core +
# surfaces"). It is a SES-to-Eagle-script converter: it reads a session file and emits an Eagle
# CAD command script, touching neither the DSN grammar nor the board. Mapped here (rather than
# left unmapped, which would print `UNMAPPED SessionToEagle`, or excluded by weakening the
# script) so its one public method is checked against the deferral marker in `lib.rs`.
SessionToEagle           lib.rs
